       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose five times the maximum. A single 1000 mg dose of sertraline could seriously harm this patient, and the risk is serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmia.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Tell me the dose you want, such as 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, and I'll enter it now. Dosing within the usual range can still be titrated later.\n- **Enter it with a hold for review.** If you believe there's an unusual indication for a higher dose, I can help you prepare the request for pharmacy or attending review. I can't enter a 1000 mg order myself.\n\nIf the issue is timing, a standard-dose order can be in place well before the family arrives. Which dose should I enter?"
      }
